        <profile name="Questoris Knight Styrix" id="14f0-91bd-5845-02b1" hidden="false" typeId="c547-1836-d8a-ff4f" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="M" typeId="e703-ecb6-5ce7-aec1">10"</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="d29d-cf75-fc2d-34a4">11</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="450-a17e-9d5e-29da">3+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="750a-a2ec-90d3-21fe">26</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="LD" typeId="58d2-b879-49c7-43bc">6+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="OC" typeId="bef7-942a-1a23-59f8">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="InSv" typeId="55a7-5b54-c60d-11dc">5+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Base" typeId="nr-base-size">109x170mm</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Grav-pinned" id="b942-a6cf-18a8-b863" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">After this unit resolves its attacks, during your Shooting phase, until the end of your opponent's next turn:
  For each enemy INFANTRY unit that was hit by an attack made by the triggering unit by graviton crusher during that shooting sequence:
    - That unit is grav-pinned.
    - While the Grav Pinned is active, subtract 2" from that unit's Move characteristic.
    - While the Grav Pinned is active, subtract 2 from that unit's Charge rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Deadly Demise" id="4f92-7f29-cda6-4d51" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When this model is destroyed, after the units embarked within it have made their emergency disembark moves, roll one D6: on a 6+, for each unit: while this unit is within 6" of this model, that unit suffers a number of mortal wounds equal to its rating.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Damaged" id="f537-7c5b-b25b-03c7" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">While the model has X or fewer wounds remaining, X being its rating, subtract 1 from this model's Hit rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Styrix's Duty" id="a0f6-33fa-9e20-7bfd" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When this unit is selected to shoot or when this unit is selected to fight or after the triggering unit resolves its attacks, while the Styrixs Duty is active:
  - Select one enemy unit that was hit by an attack made by the triggering unit during that shooting sequence. That unit must take a Battle-shock test, applying -1 to that test.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Damaged Objective Control" id="77c5-9b8b-4fb8-443c" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">While the model is Damaged, subtract its rating from this model's Objective Control characteristic.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
